      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "A nonzero minor of the matrix over the field supplies a scalar left inverse already over the original ring; no domain or flatness premise on that ring is added."
    },
    {
      "id": "GSL3",
      "block_sha256": "84fce60bc8278961f3def9072e25ccf7529f28af8b4aaed7f43247679a7b5bff",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The two denominators give literal matrix identities D0 B=0, CB=rI and BC+HD0=rI. Kernel rank zero and empty selected-column cases are included."
    },
    {
      "id": "GSL4",
      "block_sha256": "a162e8332c1e49ad19324b53924a67525651a3231afd387705930d02381baf65",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The identities prove a basis after every ring map inverting r. The field value of r is nonzero, and in a local residue-field application r is already a unit."
    },
    {
      "id": "GSL5",
      "block_sha256": "faed7922c7bc400afe83aed47641b08e0393ff440019fd08c2600f067f7ee4b2",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The finite-projective three-term complex is converted to actual finite matrices by adjoining chosen complements. The kernel and middle-exactness correspondences survive arbitrary tensor products."
    },
    {
      "id": "GSL6",
      "block_sha256": "3b6f0ada83426b296a6e7f3ecd5fd74c140856f3709a2c3868a373e1d835c647",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Descending finite cone lifts construct the bounded nonnegative finite model over a Noetherian ring. Its degree-zero module is a finite quotient and the displayed cone is exact."
    },
    {
      "id": "GSL7",
      "block_sha256": "fa1c62e4d4e5287d6fde9bd7fe36ce337be57b06616cf4c2e42099c67d401eb0",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The bounded flat cone is worked backward through short exact image sequences. This proves universal tensor exactness and finite flat degree-zero projectivity, with the dual-basis globalization made explicit."
    },
    {
      "id": "GSL8",
      "block_sha256": "529ee8a2db7e435a5961bb907d7628a5e4f1eaadab2e727db78d731c2673da02",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The nonempty cube vertices descend to the supplied Noetherian model. The resulting finite-projective complex and comparison map work over arbitrary original R; the empty-index case is handled separately."
    },
    {
      "id": "GSL9",
      "block_sha256": "c139f6c0f63b2382454e757f8244878a0c409602985899a784a286f25a86c5a4",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The Cech complex uses actual affine intersections and pulled line-bundle sections. Degree-zero gluing and the literal all-cover H1 vanishing are compared through refinement, without replacing the source condition."
    },
    {
      "id": "GSL10",
      "block_sha256": "463e288002344c9be49722fb2f2b9fd52aed1850479f012e87e923c383eeefd9",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Every Perf field, including fixed coordinate functions and the universal sec equation, is constructed. The very-ample cover has affine finite intersections by explicit section ratios; the original geometric model supplier is retained."
    },
    {
      "id": "GSL11",
      "block_sha256": "0a04e78df19612685c2b86031e694f70986dc9183fbc4f7a35b98d087e7a599d",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Linearity, uniqueness and naturality follow from Perf.sec even though the supplied maps are initially only set equivalences. This retains every prescribed Cartesian model."
    },
    {
      "id": "GSL12",
      "block_sha256": "9e6f5f10cbf243f2fe681b32efe5c9402e459503096eeb970a518a96d4ad820d",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "One denominator and actual sections are chosen before every affine test. Their cardinality is fixed by the specified field rank, with zero rank allowed."
    },
    {
      "id": "GSL13",
      "block_sha256": "4e6636cc24f9424064177e6e10f57d96266af5953b19a2fe3719a584072a064c",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "A surjective coefficient map lifts every section using the same fixed basis; the conclusion is the actual chartwise IsPullSecLC identity."
    },
    {
      "id": "GSL14",
      "block_sha256": "17533ec5d2dab660dc8181ca9cca76d7061009d0043be25c36f98347cc05e52b",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Specified scheme and bundle isomorphisms transport sections, bases and literal H1 data by units in the charts; no unrecorded identifications enter the later twist argument."
    },
    {
      "id": "GSL15",
      "block_sha256": "159aa1fc146dacda1a95500e669a23fe0c2c41131c6cb646d026444e35f40444",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Projectivity after the actual affine pullback is proved from retained PolBaseChangeSt and RelAmple data, using explicit very-ample coordinate ratios. The geometric law itself is not claimed here."
    },
    {
      "id": "GSL16",
      "block_sha256": "c51f37b54c0ea4d22cb1e0a48d72a4c7538343e724d77b6429c2fb2f0639968d",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Finite-group averaging descends the H1 cocycle when the group order is invertible. Exact invariant-function descent remains an explicit geometric premise."
    },
    {
      "id": "GSL17",
      "block_sha256": "ed9a1beba15c0534826fbcf2a7a3510462f0b27d402b57e5e871d316041aa226",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Positive-power H1 vanishing follows from retained Serre, multiplication and invariant-descent inputs. A sufficiently large prime distinct from the characteristic is chosen, and all Serre residue classes are covered."
    },
    {
      "id": "GSL18",
      "block_sha256": "400b42ce7336b85e4e44f8d3150da2a1048e4dcdd8bd60347026ae6b6a8b0ad5",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The integer growth lemma first determines square values by iteration, then uses multiplicative spacing within two integers and monotonicity to recover every h(j)=j^g; dimension zero is included."
    },
    {
      "id": "GSL19",
      "block_sha256": "87ffbba35b97ccd74e55941bb9cc8361ae9b29948d0df6fdfccf2c11671af369",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The exact rank n^g follows from retained initial rank one, actual section decomposition, multiplication identities and growth. No degree-of-multiplication assertion is silently substituted."
    },
    {
      "id": "GSL20",
      "block_sha256": "0aa74bf0437d4350214c10794d07048c5d1e7de2143b3d3f434076cf23ff7501",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The rank and H1 results transfer to every actual geometric fiber using PolBaseChange and the specified pullback maps."
    },
    {
      "id": "GSL21",
      "block_sha256": "0ac8e956b30648beb7b5782a8aaf37bc3ab60b8dd3a30762536665039d0f8d01",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Translated-power generation uses the original multiplication geometry and theorem-of-square generators. The root is chosen only in an algebraically closed fiber, including characteristic dividing q."
    },
    {
      "id": "GSL22",
      "block_sha256": "5bea63f395991fd66abdcb7647bdbbab685a397e6ae9a27ebd18fd5e5a3ac119",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The twisted geometric fiber is identified with a translated pure power through explicit maps and bundle units. The original base may be arbitrary because the root is used only over the geometric field."
    },
    {
      "id": "GSL23",
      "block_sha256": "2db53ea714d34c24119d7c9d51dd4d195cfac82340af7712434b768666b56a52",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The full conditional SecBaseChangeAny/St chooses one affine neighborhood and one set of sections before all test rings and tuples. FPerf, P, V and R are retained with their original scopes."
    },
    {
      "id": "GSL24",
      "block_sha256": "279e35b65798123d7e12db6e964272616490460034e0740bbec94d8fb1c5a9e7",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The full local twisted-basis statement uses the same matrix over the local ring and every coefficient extension. The geometric root is not lifted to that local ring; T remains an explicit premise."
    },
    {
      "id": "GSL25",
      "block_sha256": "db2332103f85b6e089cde32302056bc12cb5b7fb56892a10ba4da3eba0536a56",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Every residue section lifts on the original twist bundle and satisfies literal IsPullSecLC. Composition is written in conventional right-to-left order; arbitrary local rings and arbitrary residue sections are retained."
    },
    {
      "id": "GSL26",
      "block_sha256": "30f1a583e91594cb27f937e2eeb17f11ef6d39f94e84d4c936c20b4430cdc811",
